  ],
  "text": "About three hundred and seventy five million years ago, something with fins left the water. Fins are for swimming. They are not built to hold anything up. But this one had bones inside its fin that look a lot like a wrist. It also had a neck. Fish do not have necks. And lungs, alongside its gills. It could gulp air at the surface. The strangest part is how we found it. Someone predicted exactly where to dig. Right age of rock, right ancient shoreline. They went there, and it was there. Every land animal since is that same fin, rearranged. Roll your sleeve up. Those are the same bones, still in the same order. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
